{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the descendants of Reuben, firstborn of Israel.</b> He placed Reuben first because he is the firstborn, even though the standard of Judah precedes his standard; and after Reuben, Simeon, because that is the order of their birth; and after him, Gad, because he is the firstborn of Leah's maidservant; and after that he mentioned the standard of Judah, and after him Issachar and Zebulun, because they encamp with him; and after that he mentioned the standard of Ephraim, and after him Manasseh and Benjamin, who encamp with him; and after that he mentioned the standard of Dan, and after him Asher and Naphtali, who encamp with him; and so they are arranged in this order in the dedication of the altar. And these tribes that are numbered are twelve, for Levi and Joseph are not included, and the two sons of Joseph were in place of their father, and these tribes stood at the four directions of the world, three to each direction. And we do not find among all the tribes mighty ones like the tribe of Judah, which is likened to a lion's cub (Genesis 49:9), and like the tribe of Dan, concerning which it is likewise written (Deuteronomy 33:22) ״דן גור אריה״, and therefore they were the first and the last. And the reason he mentioned their skulls (גולגלותיהם) in the case of Reuben and Simeon and did not do so with the rest of the tribes — Scripture adopted a concise style; or because Reuben and Simeon grieved their father and needed double atonement compared to the rest of the tribes. And he added to say ״פקודיו״ in the case of Simeon, which is not so with the rest of the tribes, and I do not know why. Perhaps the word ״פקודיו״ is not an expression of number but rather a visitation of punishment, and the construal of the verse is thus: לבני שמעון פקודיו תולדותם למשפחותם לבית אבותם — 'to the descendants of Simeon, his visitations, their descendants by their families, by their fathers' houses' — and what follows below, ״במספר שמות״, is drawn together with their ״פקודיהם״ (their number), and it comes to say that the descendants of Simeon were punished by the Holy One, blessed be He, deserving that the sin of Simeon their father be visited upon them in the sale of Joseph, for he was the one who took him and cast him into the pit — from what the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded (Genesis 37:24): ״ויקחהו וישליכו אותו״, it is written ״ויקחהו״ (singular) — Simeon took him; and therefore it is written (Genesis 42:24): ״ויקח מאתם את שמעון״." "<b>And their number.</b> The count that came out here is nine and fifty thousand and three hundred, to hint that the Satan ruled over their number, and therefore when the prince of their tribe sinned, their sentence was sealed and their number was diminished until they fell to less than half the number given here. And the reason that in all the tribes he wrote לבני (\"to the descendants of\"), but in the case of Naphtali he wrote לבני נפתלי (\"to the descendants of Naphtali\"), is because the tribe of Naphtali differed from the rest of the tribes, for in the tribe of Naphtali the daughters were more numerous than the sons, and therefore in Jacob's blessing it was hinted in the feminine form (Genesis 49:21): ״נפתלי אילה שלוחה״, and because of this he wrote concerning him לבני — as one who selects the sons from among the daughters."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:41.555014192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}